"635":236,"636":242,"637":228},"orderedDocs":[[204,"**+ New panel** opens `#/guild/<id>/panel/new`"],[537,"**Admin role**\n: A higher-tier staff role. Admins additionally get **Manage Channels** inside channel tickets."],[604,"**Admin roles** are a higher tier - on channel tickets they're given **Manage Channels** inside the\nticket, and they act as the fallback when a ticket type doesn't define its own admin roles."],[575,"**Anyone curious about the settings** - the Dashboard and\nCustomization sections cover every field and button."],[538,"**Audit log**\n: A reverse-chronological record of settings, panel, blacklist and ticket changes, each with an\nactor ID and timestamp."],[539,"**Blacklist**\n: A list of users who cannot open tickets in a server."],[296,"**Blacklist** button"],[411,"**Blacklisted users** get an ephemeral \"You're not allowed to open tickets in this server\"\nmessage, with the reason if one was set."],[540,"**Button panel**\n: A panel that shows one button per ticket type (max 5)."],[285,"**Buttons** - label, emoji and style for `claim`, `add`, `remove`, `rename` and `close`."],[224,"**Buttons** - one button per type. Discord allows **5** buttons per row, so the panel shows at\nmost **5** types in this mode."],[541,"**Channel ticket**\n: A private channel created for a single ticket."],[399,"**Channel tickets** are private. The bot sets permission overwrites so that:"],[542,"**Claim**\n: A staff member marking themselves as handling a ticket."],[290,"**Closing behaviour** - DM the opener a copy, delete the channel on close."],[543,"**Customization**\n: The messages, colours, buttons and priorities that shape how tickets look and read. Set\nserver-wide, per panel, and per type."],[561,"**dat one ticketer** is a Discord ticketing bot. Users click a panel in your server, a private\nchannel or thread opens for them, and your staff manage it with buttons or slash commands. Every\nticket can be exported as an HTML transcript when it closes."],[255,"**Delete** - asks `Delete this panel and its message?`, removes the Discord message, and deletes\nthe panel and its types."],[544,"**Dropdown panel**\n: A panel that shows a select menu of ticket types (max 25)."],[223,"**Dropdown** - one select menu. Up to **25** ticket types. Best when you have several options."],[254,"**Duplicate** - copies the panel and all its types, then opens the copy so you can rename it."],[205,"**Edit** on a row opens `#/guild/<id>/panel/<pid>`"],[164,"**Footer**:"],[160,"**Header**, left to right:"],[545,"**Internal note**\n: A staff-only note on a ticket. Never shown to the opener and never included in transcripts."],[177,"**Invite the bot** in the top-right adds the bot to a new server."],[287,"**Mention pings** - ping the opener, plus comma-separated role IDs to ping."],[466,"**never** shown to the opener or included in the transcript."],[546,"**Panel**\n: A message in a channel with a dropdown or buttons that opens tickets."],[547,"**Placeholder**\n: A `{token}` in a text field that is replaced with a real value, e.g. `{username}`."],[286,"**Priorities** - add/edit/remove rows of emoji + label + id + colour."],[548,"**Priority**\n: Low / Normal / High / Urgent (or your own list). Used by the Priority button and shown on the\nwelcome embed."],[295,"**Reason (optional)** text box"],[573,"**Server owners & admins** who want to invite the bot and configure it - start with\nGetting started."],[607,"**Staff bypass these limits**, so they can always open a ticket to test."],[549,"**Staff**\n: Anyone with **Manage Channels**, or any role listed in Staff roles or Admin roles."],[413,"**Staff** bypass all open-ticket limits (they can always open a ticket to test)."],[574,"**Staff** who live in tickets - read Using tickets."],[550,"**Sub-type**\n: A second choice under a ticket type, e.g. `Bug report → Crash`."],[288,"**System messages** - claimed, renamed, member added, member removed, ticket closed, transcript\nsaved."],[551,"**Tag**\n: A short free-text label staff can put on a ticket."],[555,"**Thread ticket**\n: A private thread created for a single ticket (auto-archives after 7 days; archived + locked on\nclose)."],[405,"**Thread tickets** are private threads created under the panel's thread-parent channel (or the\npanel channel). The opener is added as a member; `invitable` is off. Threads auto-archive after\n7 days (10080 minutes) of inactivity."],[553,"**Ticket type**\n: One option on a panel, e.g. `General Support` or `Sales`."],[552,"**Ticket**\n: A single support conversation, opened from a panel and living in its own channel or thread."],[339,"**Transcript channel**, if set;"],[289,"**Transcript embed** - colour, footer, title, description."],[554,"**Transcript**\n: A styled HTML copy of a ticket's messages, generated when the ticket closes."],[294,"**User ID** text box (placeholder `123456789012345678`)"],[284,"**Welcome message** - colour, title, message, footer, thumbnail URL, image URL, and a\n`Show \"Opened by\" line` checkbox."],[102,"`{name}` in the **Renamed** message and `{userAvatar}` in the welcome fields are the intended\nplaceholders for those spots. `{note}` in **Ticket closed** is filled with the **Transcript\nsaved** text."],[400,"`@everyone` cannot view the channel."],[381,"`/about` - brand, author and contact details, plus an **Add to a server** link button."],[349,"`/blacklist`"],[370,"`/config set` keys:"],[348,"`/config`"],[380,"`/help` - a short setup guide and a pointer to the buttons inside tickets."],[350,"`/help` and `/about`"],[432,"`/panel delete` removes a panel and its types (and its message)."],[431,"`/panel list` shows every panel with its ID, channel and mode."],[430,"`/panel resend` deletes the old message (if any) and posts a new one in the panel's channel."],[346,"`/panel`"],[382,"`/panel` and `/blacklist` are staff-gated. If someone without the right role runs them they get\n`You need the **Manage Server** permission to use this command.`"],[347,"`/ticket`"],